\par\b\fs26 1. Purpose\b0\fs22\par
\par
We operate a single Google Ads account for our own auto parts business. This
tool reads reporting data from that account and displays it on an internal
management dashboard used by our own staff.
\par
Before this integration, the same numbers were imported manually from a
third-party connector. The purpose of using the API directly is accuracy and
freshness of our own reporting \u8212? not automation of campaign management.
\par
\par\b\fs26 2. Scope of access \u8212? read only\b0\fs22\par
\par
The tool performs \b no write operations of any kind\b0 . It does not create,
modify, pause or remove campaigns, ad groups, ads, keywords, budgets, bids,
audiences, conversion actions or account settings.
\par
Every call is a `GoogleAdsService.SearchStream` request. The complete set of
queries the tool issues is:
\par
\b Query 1 \u8212? daily cost and performance by campaign\b0 
\par
\f1\fs18 
SELECT campaign.id,\line
       campaign.name,\line
       segments.date,\line
       metrics.cost_micros,\line
       metrics.clicks,\line
       metrics.impressions,\line
       metrics.conversions\line
  FROM campaign\line
 WHERE segments.date BETWEEN '<start>' AND '<end>'\line
\f0\fs22 
\par
\b Query 2 \u8212? account identification (used only by the connection test)\b0 
\par
\f1\fs18 
SELECT customer.descriptive_name,\line
       customer.currency_code\line
  FROM customer\line
 LIMIT 1\line
\f0\fs22 
\par
No other resource is queried.
\par
\par\b\fs26 3. Frequency and volume\b0\fs22\par
\par
The collector runs \b once per day\b0 , as part of a scheduled routine at 07:30
(America/Sao_Paulo). Each run issues approximately \b 2 to 5 requests\b0 ,
covering the current calendar year to date.
\par
Estimated volume: \b fewer than 100 operations per day\b0 .
\par
\par\b\fs26 4. Users and distribution\b0\fs22\par
\par
The dashboard is used \b only by employees of Nevada Eco Pe\u231?as\b0  \u8212? the owner and
a small sales team. It is protected by a password login and is not offered,
sold, licensed or made available to any third party. We do not manage Google
Ads accounts for other companies, and we do not resell, redistribute or expose
the data outside the company.
\par
\par\b\fs26 5. Architecture\b0\fs22\par
\par
Layer   Description\line
Collector   Python script (`app/google_ads_api.py`), runs locally on a scheduled task\line
Transport   Google Ads API REST endpoint via standard HTTPS (`urllib`), no third-party SDK\line
Auth   OAuth 2.0 authorization code flow; refresh token generated once by the account owner\line
Storage   Results written to local JSON files, then pushed to a private Postgres database\line
Presentation   Internal web dashboard (Flask), password-protected, used by staff only\line
\par
Data flow:
\par
\f1\fs18 
Google Ads API  \u8594?  collector (local)  \u8594?  JSON  \u8594?  private database  \u8594?  internal dashboard\line
\f0\fs22 
\par
\par\b\fs26 6. Credential handling\b0\fs22\par
\par
The developer token, OAuth client ID, client secret and refresh token are
stored in a single file outside version control, on a machine controlled by the
company. They are never embedded in the application code, never sent to any
third party, and never exposed to the dashboard's users.
\par
\par\b\fs26 7. Data retained\b0\fs22\par
\par
Only aggregate advertising metrics: campaign name and ID, date, cost, clicks,
impressions and conversions. The tool does not request, receive or store any
personal data, user identifiers, or Customer Match audience data.
\par
\par\b\fs26 8. Compliance\b0\fs22\par
\par
- Read-only access; no mutate operations\line
- Data used solely for internal reporting about our own advertising spend\line
- No redistribution, resale or third-party access\line
- API contact email is a monitored inbox on the company domain\line
  (contato@nevadaautopecas.com.br)
\par
